SysTick - 24-bit down-counter inside the ARM Core. Always present, vendor-independent, needs no RCC
clock. Use this for the system tick.

A timer (TIM2-TIM7) - ST peripheral. Save these for PWM, capture, and other jobs that need pins. 

Rule of Thumb: SysTick for the tick, timers for everything else.

SysTick Registers:
At 0xE000E010, 4 Registers:

Register		Purpose
CTRL			Enable, interrupt enable, clock source, COUNTFLAG
LOAD			Reload Value (max 0x00FFFFFF)
VAL				Current Count - write anything to clear
CALIB			Calibration (ignore)

CTRL bits: 0 = Enable, 1 = TICKINT (Interrupt), 2 = CLKSOURCE (1 = Processor Clock).
It counts down. At 0, it relods from LOAD and fires SysTick_Handler.

